<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="info-section" style="background:var(--cream)">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="lbl">Common questions about cost</span>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <h2>Before you compare prices, <em>read this</em></h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Why is there such a wide price range?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-a">Because the technology is different. PRK uses a surface laser with no flap creation. LASIK adds a microkeratome flap. Femto-LASIK replaces the blade with a femtosecond laser. SMILE Pro eliminates the flap entirely using a 2mm keyhole incision on the ZEISS VisuMax 800. Each step up adds precision, safety, and faster recovery — but also cost. The right question isn't "which is cheapest" but "which is safest for my specific cornea."</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Does cheaper mean worse?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-a">Not necessarily. PRK has been performed safely for decades and is still the best option for certain eye profiles — particularly thin corneas and patients in contact sports. The issue is when a clinic offers only one technology and fits every patient into it. At El Naggar Center, Dr. El Naggar recommends the technology that matches your Pentacam results — sometimes that's the most affordable option.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">What does the price include?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-a">At our clinic, the quoted price covers the full procedure on both eyes, all pre-operative assessments, the Pentacam scan, prescribed recovery eye drops, and 12 months of follow-up appointments. There are no hidden add-ons. The initial consultation assessment is booked and priced separately from the procedure itself.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">Can I pay in instalments?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes. We work with ValU and Premium Card for instalment plans. Depending on the technology and plan length, monthly payments can start from around EGP 2,500/month. Our team can walk you through the exact options after your assessment.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button type="button" class="faq-q" onclick="toggleFaq(this)">What is a Pentacam scan and why do I need one?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
        <div class="faq-a">A Pentacam is a rotating camera that maps your entire cornea in 3D — measuring thickness, curvature, and elevation at thousands of points. It tells us definitively which technologies are safe for your specific eyes and which are not. Without it, any price estimate is just a guess. That's why we start every patient journey with one.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

